nse. In dev: `vinext dev` via vite config with cloudflare plugin. Assets via the ASSETS binding.\n\n- app/page.tsx is a client component (\"use client\") and manages progress via localStorage key \"assistant-study-progress\". The percent is computed from `completed.length / stages.length` — note: it's the number of stages, not the number of items.\n\n- Verification commands:\n  - `npm run typecheck` → tsc --noEmit\n  - `npm run lint` → eslint .\n  - `npm test` → build + node --test tests/rendered-html.test.mjs (SSR smoke test of built output)\n  - `npm run build` → vinext build\n  - `npm run benchmark:validate` → validates schema, T1 task/prompt/rubric (100 points), T2/T3 write tasks including private suite hashes and seeded failing commands, and the @AGENTS.md reference in CLAUDE.md\n  - `npm run benchmark:env` → records environment JSON\n  - `npm run benchmark:run -- ...` → preview (default) or execute\n  - `npm run verify` → typecheck + lint + test + benchmark:validate\n  - `npm run dev`, `npm run start`, `npm run db:generate`\n\n- Risks:\n  1. The benchmark contracts are frozen, but RESUME.md says the prepared changes (opencode.json's OpenRouter entry, the runner's access path change) are uncommitted — meaning there may be uncommitted state. Evidence: RESUME.md's \"exact next steps\" item 1 says \"intentionally commit the prepared setup docs, OpenCode provider entries, and benchmark runner access path changes.\" Also benchmark/environment/2026-08-22T19-04-16.602Z.json is committed (an environment snapshot inside the repo — a committed environment record is unusual but probably intentional).\n  2. `benchmark/private/*` is git-ignored, but benchmark-validate.mjs requires the existence of the private suites locally. On a fresh clone, `npm run benchmark:validate` (and therefore `verify`) fails because the private suites are missing. Evidence: lines 46-72 of the validate script assert existsSync of the private suites. This is a real onboarding risk: on a fresh clone,