{"type":"text","timestamp":1787458513246,"sessionID":"ses_fd32dbadbffeNokwlDABHEwXNJ","part":{"id":"prt_02cd4113d001e7xPvJT10Rtndh","messageID":"msg_02cd3b613002BLV0VMcatm443D","sessionID":"ses_fd32dbadbffeNokwlDABHEwXNJ","type":"text","text":"\n\n## Architecture\n\nThis repo has two coupled parts, both described in `README.md` and `AGENTS.md`:\n\n1. **Interactive study page** — a single-page Next.js 16 (App Router) + React 19 site, rendered through **vinext** (a Vite-based Next runtime) on **Cloudflare Workers** (`worker/index.ts`, `@cloudflare/vite-plugin` in `vite.config.ts`, `wrangler` devDeps). `app/layout.tsx` sets metadata/fonts; `app/page.tsx` (1,123 lines) is one `\"use client\"` component holding all content as module-level arrays (`assistantCards`, `modelRows`, `benchmarkLanes`, `taskRows`, `scoreRows`, `stages`, `sources`) plus localStorage-backed progress. Styling is Tailwind 4 + hand-rolled `app/globals.css`.\n2. **Benchmark harness** — a reproducible study comparing coding assistants/models per the frozen contract `benchmark/STUDY.md`. Key directories:\n   - `benchmark/tasks/{T1-repo-map,T2-filter-valid-runs,T3-comparison-summary}/` — versioned `prompt.md`, `task.json`, `rubric.json`.\n   - `benchmark/schemas/` — JSON Schemas for task/run/result.\n   - `benchmark/fixtures/` — T2/T3 working code with visible tests; `benchmark/private/` — git-ignored hidden test suites (see `benchmark/private/README.md`).\n   - `benchmark/reports/` — pilot result write-ups; `benchmark/runs/` — git-ignored run evidence.\n   - `scripts/benchmark-env.mjs`, `benchmark-validate.mjs`, `benchmark-run.mjs` — environment capture, contract validation, and the run executor (isolated detached Git worktrees, per-assistant adapters, before/after workspace snapshots, `result.json`).\n   - `opencode.json` — checked-in OpenCode provider config (Ollama, OpenRouter Qwen).\n\nScaffolding that is currently inert: `db/schema.ts` is intentionally empty, `db/index.ts` defines a D1 `getDb()`, `.openai/hosting.json` has `d1: null, r2: null`, and `examples/d1/` is opt-in sample code. `app/chatgpt-auth.ts` is a template auth helper with no importers (verified by grep).\n\n## Main request flow\n\nA browser `GET /` flows: Cloudflare Worker `fetch` in `worker/index.ts:29` → path is not `/_vinext/image`, so it delegates to `vinext/server/app-router-entry` (`worker/index.ts:43`) → the RSC app router renders `app/layout.tsx`, which wraps `app/page.tsx` (server-rendered, then client-hydrated; on mount it reads `assistant-study-progress` from `window.localStorage`, `app/page.tsx:393-410`) → HTML response. Static assets (JS/CSS bundles, `public/favicon.svg`) are served via the `ASSETS` binding configured in `vite.config.ts`. The test in `tests/rendered-html.test.mjs:4-22` simulates exactly this boundary by calling the built worker (`dist/server/index.js`) with a fake `Request` and `ASSETS` binding.\n\n## Verification\n\nFrom `package.json` scripts:\n\n- `npm run typecheck` — `tsc --noEmit`; strict-typechecks all TS/TSX (app, worker, db, examples, build plugins).\n- `npm run lint` — ESLint 9 with `eslint-config-next` vitals + TypeScript; proves style/rule compliance.\n- `npm test` — `npm run build && node --test tests/rendered-html.test.mjs`; builds the production bundle, then smoke-tests the built worker: HTTP 200, `text/html`, expected content strings, and absence of skeleton/preview markers.\n- `npm run build` — `vinext build`; proves the production worker + assets compile (also packages `.openai` metadata via `build/sites-vite-plugin.ts`).\n- `npm run benchmark:validate` — asserts schemas are draft-2020-12, T1 is read-only with the five required headings and a 100-point rubric, T2/T3 write tasks have correct allowed paths, hidden suites exist with matching SHA-256 and still fail (seeded bugs intact), and `CLAUDE.md` starts with `@AGENTS.md`.\n- `npm run benchmark:env` — prints (or with `--write`, records) tool versions, hardware, and Git state; deliberately excludes credentials.\n- `npm run benchmark:run -- --assistant <x>` — safe preview printing the exact command; `--execute` performs a recorded run in an isolated worktree.\n- `npm run verify` — typecheck + lint + test + benchmark:validate; the full gate.\n- `npm run dev` / `npm run start` — local vinext server. `npm run db:generate` — drizzle-kit, a no-op until a schema exists.\n\n## Risks and unknowns\n\n1. **Fresh clones cannot pass `verify`.** Evidence: `scripts/benchmark-validate.mjs:58-72` requires the hidden suites under `benchmark/private/`, but `.gitignore:46-47` ignores everything there except the README. Inference: validation of the committed contract depends on untracked local files; a newcomer or CI without those files will see `benchmark:validate` (and `verify`) fail.\n2. **Frozen study content is duplicated.** Evidence: `benchmark/STUDY.md` and the arrays in `app/page.tsx` both encode lanes, tasks, and the scorecard, with minor wording drift (\"Explanation and handoff\" vs \"Explanation\"); `AGENTS.md` forbids changing `STUDY.md` except in a new study version. Inference: any contract change needs synchronized edits in frozen evidence and UI, with drift risk.\n3. **Dirty baseline before recorded runs.** Evidence: `RESUME.md` \"Exact next steps\" item 1 says the OpenRouter provider entry and runner access-path change are prepared but not committed, and `benchmark-run.mjs:416-417` refuses to run when tracked changes exist. Inference: this checkout may be ahead of its last commit; a pilot run requires an intentional commit first. Secondary: unused scaffolding (`app/chatgpt-auth.ts`, `db/`, `examples/d1/`) enlarges the typecheck/lint surface without providing functionality.\n\n## Small change plan\n\nAdd a visible \"pilot completed\" status to the study page:\n\n1. **Fix semantics without touching frozen files.** Keep the status static in UI data inside `app/page.tsx` (e.g., a constant near the other arrays); do not edit `benchmark/STUDY.md`, which is frozen evidence.\n2. **Implement.** Render an accessible label (e.g., a pill in the `header` next to `.mini-progress` at `app/page.tsx:454-460`, or in the hero) reading \"Pilot completed\"; add any needed class to `app/globals.css` following its existing custom-property conventions.\n3. **Cover it in the smoke test.** Extend `tests/rendered-html.test.mjs` with an assertion like `assert.match(html, /Pilot completed/)` so the built output is checked.\n4. **Run focused checks.** `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint`, then `npm test` (builds and renders the page).\n5. **Full gate and scope review.** Run `npm run verify`, then confirm via `git status` that only `app/page.tsx`, `app/globals.css`, and the test changed — no `benchmark/` files, per the frozen-evidence rule.","time":{"start":1787458490685,"end":1787458513240}}}
